# {{.project_name}}

API + mobile workspace generated by smokeforge.

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `apps/api` | Go or Rust API; owns persistence, auth, and business rules |
| `apps/android` | Android Compose client, when selected |
| `apps/ios` | SwiftUI client, when selected |
| `CONTEXT-MAP.md` | Where to find project context and boundaries |

## Code layout

```text
apps/
  api/                 Go or Rust API, its Dockerfile, tests, and docs
  android/             Android Compose client, when selected
  ios/                 SwiftUI client, when selected
.github/workflows/     root CI aggregation
CONTEXT-MAP.md         API/mobile context boundary and runtime flow
Makefile               one entry point for install, dev, test, and CI
```

Only selected app folders are present. `make mobile-build` and
`make mobile-test` run the mobile targets that exist.

## First run

```bash
make install
make api-dev   # API on http://localhost:8080
make mobile-build
```

Android uses `http://10.0.2.2:8080` from the emulator. iOS uses
`http://127.0.0.1:8080` from the simulator. Both are compile-time API
configuration values in the generated app.

iOS requires macOS, Xcode 26.6, and XcodeGen. `project.yml` is the source of
truth; `make ios-project` generates the Xcode project.

See each app's `README.md` and `CONTEXT.md` before changing it.
